WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:02.801
-Today is Friday, and that's
usually when I catch up

00:00:02.801 --> 00:00:03.870
with some personal stuff.

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.138
I check my inbox,
I return some e-mails,

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:07.240
and, of course,
I send out thank you notes.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.075
I was just running a bit behind,

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:10.710
so I'd like to write out
some right now.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:12.745
James, can I get some thank you
note-writing music, please?

00:00:12.745 --> 00:00:15.781 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:15.781 --> 00:00:16.882
Fantastic.

00:00:16.882 --> 00:00:18.218
-He's humming
the "Curly Shuffle."

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:19.351
-Doesn't even look at
the keys anymore.

00:00:19.351 --> 00:00:20.553
-Yeah, he doesn't even need it.

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:21.921
-He knows the...
-I don't think he's playing it.

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:26.225
-He finally learned the song.
-Yeah.

00:00:26.225 --> 00:00:27.660 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:31.197
Thank you, Beyoncé's new song,
"Break My Soul,"

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:33.599
or as Adele put it, "A song
that breaks your soul?

00:00:33.599 --> 00:00:34.868
Stay in your lane, girl."

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:36.970
[ Applause ]

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:42.208
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:43.876
Thank you,

00:00:43.876 --> 00:00:47.413
Hostess' new cryptocurrency
themed snack cake,

00:00:47.413 --> 00:00:48.615
$TWINKcoin...

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:50.716
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.716 --> 00:00:52.919
...for telling the world
you know what crypto is,

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:54.988
but you don't know what
Urban Dictionary is.

00:00:54.988 --> 00:00:57.023
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:03.830
-Give us two Twinkcoin.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:06.666
-Uh...

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:09.268
Thank you, sending
your kids to summer camp

00:01:09.268 --> 00:01:12.505
for basically saying, "Here,
they're your problem now."

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:14.607
[ Applause ]

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:17.042
Do whatever.

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:22.247
I like this one.
-You like this one?

00:01:22.247 --> 00:01:24.551
-Thank you, trucker hats,

00:01:24.551 --> 00:01:27.587
for just being regular hats
with a screened-in back porch.

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:29.789
[ Applause ]

00:01:35.661 --> 00:01:39.299
Thank you, COVID vaccines
for kids under 5

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:41.901
for finally making it okay
to cough on a baby again.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:44.337
[ Laughter ]
-What?

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:46.806
-[ Coughing ]

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:49.142
[ Imitates baby crying ]

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:51.344
-Thank you, lightbulbs,

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:53.746
for being a very old idea
that gets to be the symbol

00:01:53.746 --> 00:01:56.282
of all new ideas.

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:57.951
[ Applause ]

00:01:59.585 --> 00:02:03.856
-I grok. That's deep.

00:02:03.856 --> 00:02:07.459
-Thank you, going to the beach,
for being 15 minutes of fun

00:02:07.459 --> 00:02:10.029
followed by 6 weeks of finding
loose patches of sand

00:02:10.029 --> 00:02:11.297
on your body.

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:13.433
Ahh! Still?

00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:21.841
Thank you, waterslides, for
letting me know what it's like

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.242
to be flushed.

00:02:23.242 --> 00:02:25.078
There you have it, everybody!
Those are thank you notes!

